0..70 Comment "//! A fold over a type whose rule drops a variable respects that rule."
71..74 Comment "//!"
75..148 Comment "//! A choice under the high bit is its first word, and the rule drops the"
149..228 Comment "//! second word. A fold reads each field by a call of its own. So the left side"
229..308 Comment "//! of the rule holds a call at the second word, and the right side holds none."
309..312 Comment "//!"
313..387 Comment "//! The check reads the call of the fold at each variable of a rule as one"
388..466 Comment "//! value. A fold into a returner with pure effects gives each term one value,"
467..544 Comment "//! so that value stands for the call on the two sides. The kernel builds the"
545..578 Comment "//! same reading by its own code."
579..582 Comment "//!"
583..599 Comment "//! - see: #8367"
600..679 Comment "//! - see: `pathological/desc/fold-drops-variable.gandr` — the folds that the"
680..698 Comment "//!   rule refuses"
699..777 Comment "//! - see: `model/desc/family-with-rules.gandr` — the fragment and its rules"
779..805 Comment "// `Width` and `Fragment`."
